Īśādhāra,
(1) n. of a nāga, Mironovʼs reading for Iśā˚ Mvy 〔3333〕;
(2) m. pl., n. of a range of mountains (= Īṣā˚; see under Īṣādhara): Śikṣ 〔246.4〕 ˚rā(ḥ).

Īṣādhāra, m. (see under prec.),
(1) n. of a mountain or mountain-range: Divy 〔217.12, 14〕; MSV 〔i.94.6〕;
(2) n. of a deity (giving rain): Śikṣ 〔247.7〕 (or may be Iṣā˚; samdhi ambiguous);
(3) implied by Tib. instead of Iśādhāra, q.v.
